    <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
      <body>
        <div rend="parallel">
            <p xml:id="Aink449-kilavi">pācaṟaikkaṇ vēntaṉoṭu viṉaipporuṭṭāl pōntirunta talaimakaṉ avvēntaṉ māṟṟuvēntar tarutiṟaikoṇṭu mīḷvāṉākap poruntuḻit tāṉum mīṭcikkut tēr camaitta  ellaik kaṇṇē avvaracaṉ poruttam tavirntu mīṇṭum viṉaimēṟ koṇṭāṉākac colliyatu.</p>
            <p xml:lang="en">The hero, who had gone and was with the king in the warcamp for the sake of the work, after that king had taken the tribute given by the opposing king, when it was agreed that he would return, at the point when he too (the hero) had readied the chariot for return and that king abandoned the agreement and took up the work [of battle] again, spoke [this].</p>
              </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
          <lg xml:id="Aink449">        
            <l>murampukaṇ ṇuṭaiyat tiriyun tikiriyoṭu</l>
            <l>paṇainilai muṇaiiya vayamāp puṇarntu</l>
            <l>tiṇṇitiṉ māṇṭaṉṟu tērē</l>
            <l>yoṇṇutaṟ kāṇkuvam vēntuviṉai viṭiṉē.</l>
        </lg>  
 <lg xml:lang="en">                    
<l>With wheels that turn so to break the gravel,</l>
<l>joined to strong horses that hate standing in the stable,</l>
<l>the chariot is excellent in its strength.</l>
<l>We shall see the one with the bright forehead if the king frees [us] from the task.</l> 
</lg>                      
        </div>
      </body>
    </text>
